## Registering a Starlight Link Card Component

To allow authors to create visual navigation cards pointing to other articles in the CMS, the `linkcard` editor component provides a dropdown populated with existing articles:

<Tabs>
  <TabItem label="Component Registration" icon="seti:javascript">
    *Registering `<LinkCard>` with an article selection dropdown.*

    ```javascript
    CMS.registerEditorComponent({
      id: 'linkcard',
      label: 'Starlight Link Card',
      fields: [
        {
          name: 'href',
          label: 'Target Article',
          widget: 'select',
          options: getArticleSelectOptions()
        },
        { name: 'title', label: 'Card Title (Optional)', widget: 'string', required: false },
        { name: 'description', label: 'Card Description (Optional)', widget: 'string', required: false }
      ],
      pattern: /^<LinkCard\s+[^>]*?\/>/,
      fromBlock: function (match) {
        /* Extracts title, href, and description */
      },
      toBlock: function (obj) {
        return `<LinkCard title="${obj.title}" href="${obj.href}" description="${obj.description}" />`;
      },
      toPreview: function (obj) {
        /* Renders Starlight card preview in CMS editor */
      }
    });
    ```
  </TabItem>

  <TabItem label="Resulting MDX Output" icon="seti:markdown">
    *How the card saves into the document.*

    ```mdx
    <LinkCard
      title="Voice, Tone & Accessibility"
      href="/guides/voice-tone-accessibility/"
      description="Guidelines for writing clear, approachable software documentation."
    />
    ```
  </TabItem>
</Tabs>
